 an alloy of copper and zinc.","source":"File 2 General, printed question 441","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[],"id":"3b6f06d8-7124-45f8-8ad0-ea616e7bcd35","subject_id":"a1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"}},{"entry":614,"status":"INSERT","question_id":"59c1253b-fc02-4d49-824e-f2d7d4459492","source":{"entry":614,"stem":"Factor a⁴ − b⁴.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"(a − b)⁴","is_correct":false},{"label":"B","text":"(a − b)(a + b)(a² + b²)","is_correct":true},{"label":"C","text":"(a² + b²)²","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"(a − b)(a² + b²)","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Apply the difference-of-squares identity twice.","source":"File 2 General, printed question 442","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[]},"record":{"entry":614,"stem":"Factor a⁴ − b⁴.","options":[{"label":"A","text":"(a − b)⁴","is_correct":false},{"label":"B","text":"(a − b)(a + b)(a² + b²)","is_correct":true},{"label":"C","text":"(a² + b²)²","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"(a − b)(a² + b²)","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Apply the difference-of-squares identity twice.","source":"File 2 General, printed question 442","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[],"id":"59c1253b-fc02-4d49-824e-f2d7d4459492","subject_id":"83e951c5-9e30-47c7-8848-a7c7f9abb484"}},{"entry":615,"status":"INSERT","question_id":"7b713b6b-85a1-48d0-8c82-f8f78047295a","source":{"entry":615,"stem":"Which expression equals 2mx² − ny + nx + 2my²?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"2m(x + y)² + n(x − y)","is_correct":false},{"label":"B","text":"2m(x² + y²) − n(x + y)","is_correct":false},{"label":"C","text":"2m(x² + y²) + n(x − y)","is_correct":true},{"label":"D","text":"2m(x² − y²) + n(x + y)","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Grouping the m terms and n terms yields 2m(x² + y²) + n(x − y).","source":"File 2 General, printed question 443","editorial_status":"Reconstructed practice","provenance":"Newly worded practice question based on the damage