 solvent per mole of solute","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"Moles of solute per litre of solution","is_correct":true}],"explanation":"Molarity uses the total solution volume in litres.","source":"File 2 Science, printed question 69","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[],"id":"de12fd05-c88d-4c76-987d-37913c0990ed","subject_id":"a1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001"}},{"entry":690,"status":"INSERT","question_id":"ccb8d1e6-79ed-40e2-ad17-33d73691af80","source":{"entry":690,"stem":"The translational inertia of a body depends on what?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mass","is_correct":true},{"label":"B","text":"Colour","is_correct":false},{"label":"C","text":"Temperature alone","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"Volume alone","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Mass measures a body’s resistance to changes in translational motion.","source":"File 2 Science, printed question 70","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[]},"record":{"entry":690,"stem":"The translational inertia of a body depends on what?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mass","is_correct":true},{"label":"B","text":"Colour","is_correct":false},{"label":"C","text":"Temperature alone","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"Volume alone","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Mass measures a body’s resistance to changes in translational motion.","source":"File 2 Science, printed question 70","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[],"id":"ccb8d1e6-79ed-40e2-ad17-33d73691af80","subject_id":"439d7f25-5f12-49ff-84f6-6d161b79a4a9"}},{"entry":691,"status":"INSERT","question_id":"70268d84-1b60-45bd-b610-f50f97ea2c2e","source":{"entry":691,"stem":"Which pair contains one vector quantity and one scalar quantity?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Force and momentum","is_correct":false},{"label":"B","text":"Force and velocity","is_correct":false},{"label":"C","text":"Force and speed","is_correct":true},{"label":"D","text":"Force and acceleration","is_corre