_correct":false},{"label":"B","text":"100","is_correct":false},{"label":"C","text":"8","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"1,024","is_correct":true}],"explanation":"The binary unit KiB equals 2¹⁰ bytes; the SI prefix kilo means 1,000.","source":"File 2 Science, printed question 74","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[],"id":"55f42b94-7ccc-4c77-9ca2-8709fe267e00","subject_id":"83e951c5-9e30-47c7-8848-a7c7f9abb484"}},{"entry":695,"status":"INSERT","question_id":"6492c886-5091-489c-bd0f-7e615cc1cfa1","source":{"entry":695,"stem":"What is the exact SI value of Boltzmann’s constant?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1.380649 × 10⁻²³ J/K","is_correct":true},{"label":"B","text":"6.62607015 × 10⁻³⁴ J·s","is_correct":false},{"label":"C","text":"1.602176634 × 10⁻¹⁹ C","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"6.67430 × 10⁻¹¹ N·m²/kg²","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Boltzmann’s constant relates thermal energy to temperature.","source":"File 2 Science, printed question 75","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[]},"record":{"entry":695,"stem":"What is the exact SI value of Boltzmann’s constant?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"1.380649 × 10⁻²³ J/K","is_correct":true},{"label":"B","text":"6.62607015 × 10⁻³⁴ J·s","is_correct":false},{"label":"C","text":"1.602176634 × 10⁻¹⁹ C","is_correct":false},{"label":"D","text":"6.67430 × 10⁻¹¹ N·m²/kg²","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Boltzmann’s constant relates thermal energy to temperature.","source":"File 2 Science, printed question 75","editorial_status":null,"provenance":null,"references":[],"id":"6492c886-5091-489c-bd0f-7e615cc1cfa1","subject_id":"439d7f25-5f12-49ff-84f6-6d161b79a4a9"}},{"entry":696,"status":"INSERT","question_id":"1eb612f8-1ff3-4596-8e84-877403046660","source":{"entry":696,"stem":"What is the inductive reactance of an ideal inductor of inductance L at frequency f?","options":[{"label":"A","text":"X_L = 1/(2πfL)","is_correct":false},{"label":"B","text":"X_L = 2πfL","is_